---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { REPO_URL, withBase } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About" description="What THALASSA is, what the subtitle means, and who is making it.">
  <section class="section wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Ship's papers</p>
    <h1>About THALASSA</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        THALASSA is a first-person submarine game in development for one to eight players. You live aboard one large
        vessel, travel an ocean that is by turns beautiful, useful and frightening, and decide for yourselves what the
        evening is about: mapping a trench, recording a sound nobody can identify, hauling salvage, patching a leak, or
        sitting in the observation lounge and watching the water.
      </p>
      <p>
        The plan is a free game with no microtransactions and no paid servers. Co-op is designed in from the start, and a
        solo player gets an AI crew to run the ship alongside them.
      </p>

      <p>
        It is set on <a href={withBase('/world/')}>an ocean world</a> where humanity has lived beneath the waves for generations.
      </p>

      <h2>Why "Beep. Bloop."?</h2>
      <p>
        Beep is the ship: consoles, relays, confirmation chirps, the sound of machinery you have learned to trust. Bloop is
        the ocean: a name borrowed from a real and very loud underwater sound recorded in 1997, and a good summary of how
        much of the sea we still have to take on faith.
      </p>

      <h2>The tone</h2>
      <p>
        A serious world with serious stakes, and room for a little dry humour from people who have been at sea too long.
        The ship's computer may have an optional attitude setting. It will never joke during a hull breach.
      </p>

      <h2>What exists today</h2>
      <p>
        Mostly plans and experiments. The features described on this site are design intent unless a devlog entry says
        otherwise, and the <a href={REPO_URL}>source repository</a> is the place to check.
      </p>

      <h2>Bad Ideas Works</h2>
      <p>THALASSA is made by Bad Ideas Works. The name is a warning and a method.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 2.5vw, 3.2rem); }
</style>
